      {
        "id": 143332,
        "name": "pppery",
        "username": "pppery",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/3d9bf3/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-02T15:58:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Arcanist Lupus\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Arcanist Lupus:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Powerhound_2000 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Not as bad as the Ennead since there is an alernate win condition but advanced Gloomweaver against&nbsp;Legacy, The Wraith, and Parse in Megalopolis leaves you with a long game. &nbsp;As it leaves you only with the option of taking out his relics or letting him flip. &nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nWhich, if one of the Relics is eaten by the Final Wasteland while Unforgiving Wasteland is in play, becomes rather... difficult. &nbsp;This scenario is technically still winnable, because the Mongolian Death Worm deals the highest HP target 3 Toxic Damage. &nbsp;But it would take a very, very long time. &nbsp;And if the Mongolian Death Worm is taken out by the Horrid Skunk-Ape, then it too would be lost and the game would become unwinnable.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Because there are fewer than eight horrid skunk apes, this situation can only happen if the heroes either poorly communicate or deliberately leave the worm with 1 or 2 hp. Additionally, if there is only one hero alive and no villan targets other than gloomweaver, the cold damage from the amobinable snowman will get through, although.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
